      "sharpenedIdea": "A freelance bookkeeping service that handles the financial back-office for local restaurants — reconciling accounts, tracking expenses, generating P&L reports, and keeping owners tax-ready — so they can focus on running their kitchens.",
      "mvpDefinition": "Version 1 is a one-person bookkeeping practice serving 2–5 local restaurant clients on a monthly retainer. Core deliverables are: monthly bank and credit card reconciliation, restaurant-specific expense categorization (food & beverage COGS, labor, POS fees, delivery fees), and a simple monthly P&L summary report. Clients are signed through direct outreach and referrals. All client work is reviewed by the founder before delivery. Everything else — upsells, team growth, software integrations — comes after the first paying clients are locked in.",
